{"phago": "<figure class=\"fig small\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 330 528\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Phagocytosis in four stages, each in its own panel. 1 Chemotaxis: a phagocyte with a nucleus moves towards chemicals released by a bacterium. 2 Recognition and binding: receptors on the phagocyte bind to antigens on the bacterium. 3 Engulfing: the surface membrane of the phagocyte folds round the bacterium with pseudopodia. 4 Digestion and antigen display: the bacterium is inside a phagosome, a lysosome has fused with the phagosome and its enzymes break the bacterium into pieces, and antigens from it are displayed on the surface of the cell.\"><text class=\"tl tb\" x=\"8\" y=\"14\">1  Chemotaxis</text><text class=\"tl tb\" x=\"8\" y=\"146\">2  Recognition and binding</text><text class=\"tl tb\" x=\"8\" y=\"278\">3  Engulfing (endocytosis)</text><text class=\"tl tb\" x=\"8\" y=\"410\">4  Digestion and antigen display</text><path class=\"f1 s-acc sw2\" d=\"M93.2 74L93.7 76.8L93.6 79.6L93.1 82.3L92.1 84.9L90.7 87.4L89 89.6L87.1 91.5L85 93.3L83 95L80.9 96.5L78.8 97.9L76.6 99.3L74.4 100.5L72 101.6L69.6 102.4L67.1 103L64.6 103.2L62 103.2L59.5 103L57 102.6L54.5 102L52.1 101.3L49.6 100.6L47.1 99.7L44.7 98.8L42.2 97.6L39.8 96.2L37.6 94.5L35.6 92.5L34.1 90.1L32.9 87.6L32.3 84.8L32.1 82L32.2 79.3L32.6 76.6L33.2 74L33.9 71.5L34.5 69.2L35.1 66.8L35.7 64.4L36.3 62L37 59.6L37.9 57.1L39.1 54.8L40.5 52.5L42.3 50.5L44.3 48.8L46.6 47.3L49 46.1L51.5 45.2L54.1 44.4L56.7 43.9L59.3 43.5L62 43.2L64.7 43.2L67.4 43.5L70 44L72.6 44.9L75 46.2L77.1 47.8L79.1 49.6L80.8 51.7L82.2 53.8L83.5 55.9L84.8 58L86 60.1L87.3 62.2L88.7 64.3L90 66.5L91.3 68.8L92.4 71.3Z\"/><circle class=\"fm s-acc sw2\" cx=\"66\" cy=\"72\" r=\"10\"/><rect class=\"f2 s-acc2 sw2\" x=\"120\" y=\"66\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\"/><circle class=\"fh s-mute sw2\" cx=\"102\" cy=\"60\" r=\"2.5\"/><circle class=\"fh s-mute sw2\" cx=\"110\" cy=\"72\" r=\"2.5\"/><circle class=\"fh s-mute sw2\" cx=\"104\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2.5\"/><circle cl